    `there is reasonable opportunity to have recourse to the protection of a public authority in the circumstances` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes there is danger to the body of himself or any other person arising from an act which is an offence against the human body or an attempt or a threat to commit it` IS FALSE
    `that belief of danger continues` IS FALSE
    `the assault causes the defender to reasonably believe that death would be caused to him or to any other person` IS FALSE
    `the defender cannot effectually exercise the right without risk of harm to an innocent person` IS FALSE
    `harm is caused to an innocent person in the exercise of the right` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes death will otherwise be the consequence of the assault` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes grievous hurt will otherwise be the consequence of the assault` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes the assault is done with the intention of committing rape as described in section 375 or of causing such rape to be committed` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes the assault is done with the intention of causing penile penetration as described in section 376(2)` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes the assault is done with the intention of kidnapping or abducting` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes the assault is done with the intention of wrongfully confining a person in circumstances reasonably causing him to believe he will be unable to have recourse to a public authority for his release` IS FALSE
    `the defender voluntarily causes death to the assailant or wrongdoer` IS FALSE
    `the defender reasonably believes there was a danger to property of himself or any other person arising from an act which is theft robbery mischief or criminal trespass or an attempt to commit such an offence` IS FALSE
    `the offence defended against is theft` IS FALSE
    `the offender has effected his retreat with the property` IS FALSE
    `the assistance of a public authority is obtained` IS FALSE
    `the property has been recovered` IS FALSE
    `the offence defended against is robbery` IS FALSE
    `the offender causes or attempts to cause death or hurt or wrongful restraint or the fear of instant death or instant hurt or instant personal restraint continues` IS FALSE
    `the offence defended against is criminal trespass or mischief` IS FALSE
    `the offender continues in the commission of the criminal trespass or mischief` IS FALSE
    `the offence defended against is house-breaking` IS FALSE
    `the house-breaking continues` IS FALSE
    `the house-breaking was committed after 7 p.m. and before 7 a.m.` IS FALSE
    `the wrongdoer enters or leaves through a passage made by the wrongdoer or by an abettor of the house-breaking in order to commit it` IS FALSE
    `the wrongdoer enters or leaves through a passage not intended by any other person for human entrance or to which access was obtained by scaling or climbing over a wall or building` IS FALSE
    `the wrongdoer enters or leaves through a passage opened in order to commit the house-breaking by means by which the occupier did not intend it to be opened` IS FALSE
    `the wrongdoer enters or leaves by opening any lock in order to commit the house-breaking or to leave the house after one` IS FALSE
    `the wrongdoer effects his entry or leaving by using criminal force or committing an assault or by threatening any person with assault` IS FALSE
    `the wrongdoer enters or leaves by a passage he knows to have been fastened against such entry or leaving and to have been unfastened by himself or by an abettor` IS FALSE
    `the danger is mischief by fire on a building tent container or vessel used as a human dwelling or as a place for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the danger is theft mischief or house-breaking in circumstances where the defender reasonably believes death or grievous hurt will be the consequence if the right is not exercised` IS FALSE
    `the act defended against is done or attempted by a public servant acting in good faith under the actual or apparent authority of his office` IS FALSE
    `the act defended against is done or attempted by the direction of a public servant acting in good faith under the actual or apparent authority of that public servant office` IS FALSE
    `the act causes the defender to reasonably believe that death or grievous hurt would result` IS FALSE
    `the defender knows or has reason to believe that the person doing the act is such a public servant` IS FALSE
    `the defender knows or has reason to believe that the person doing the act is acting by such direction` IS FALSE
    `the person doing the act states the authority under which he acts or produces his written authority if demanded` IS FALSE

`blank exception facts` MEANS `Exception Facts` WITH
    `bound by law to do it or justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
    `is a judge acting judicially in the exercise of a power given or believed in good faith to be given by law` IS FALSE
